IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sga-time`

-- sga-part4-6.l4: Parts 4 to 6 (sections 33 to 58) of the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992 (Commonwealth),
-- Federal Register compilation C2026C00272, plain-text conversion (not the authorised text).
-- Part 4: voluntary disclosure statements and assessments. Part 5: administration. Part 6: unpaid charge, public officers, service on companies and trusts.
-- The general interest charge itself is worked out under Part IIA of the Taxation Administration Act 1953, which is not among the sources: the charge for a day is a plain input.

§ `Part 4: voluntary disclosure statements (section 33)`

-- src:998 | (1) An employer who has a superannuation guarantee shortfall for a QE day may lodge a statement about that shortfall.
@ref s 33(1) (src:998-998)
GIVEN `the employer has a superannuation guarantee shortfall for the QE day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer may lodge a statement about the shortfall` MEANS
    IF `the employer has a superannuation guarantee shortfall for the QE day` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:999 | (2) The statement is a voluntary disclosure statement if it:
-- src:1000 | (a) is lodged before the day an assessment is made for the employer for the QE day; and
-- src:1001 | (b) is in the approved form.
-- src:1002 | Note: A statement is voluntary. Lodging a statement in the approved form can reduce the employer’s administrative uplift amount of the employer’s superannuation guarantee shortfall for the QE day (see subsection 19B(3)).
@ref s 33(2) (src:999-1002)
GIVEN `the day the statement is lodged` IS A DATE
      `the day an assessment is made for the employer for the QE day` IS A DATE
      `the statement is in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a statement is a voluntary disclosure statement` MEANS
    `a statement is lodged before the day an assessment is made` `the day the statement is lodged` `the day an assessment is made for the employer for the QE day`
    AND `the statement is in the approved form`

-- src:1003 | (3) Without limiting subsection (2), the voluntary disclosure statement may include either or both of the following:
-- src:1004 | (a) the day (the receipt day) an eligible contribution made by the employer for the benefit of an employee was received by the relevant fund, RSA, representative or scheme;
-- src:1005 | (b) the day (the payment day) the contribution was paid, or debited, from an account (however described) belonging to:
-- src:1006 | (i) the employer; or
-- src:1007 | (ii) a person who is making the contribution on behalf of the employer.
@ref s 33(3) (src:1003-1007)
GIVEN item IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a voluntary disclosure statement may include` MEANS
    IF elem item (LIST "the receipt day of an eligible contribution", "the payment day of an eligible contribution")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1008 | (4) In this section:
-- src:1009 | account includes an account held with an ADI (within the meaning of the Banking Act 1959).
@ref s 33(4) (src:1008-1009)
GIVEN `it is an account held with an ADI within the meaning of the Banking Act 1959` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is an account for the purposes of section 33` MEANS
    IF `it is an account held with an ADI within the meaning of the Banking Act 1959` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Part 4: assessments and their amendment (sections 36 to 42)`

-- src:1012 | (1) The Commissioner may at any time make an assessment of the amount of:
-- src:1013 | (a) an employer’s superannuation guarantee shortfall for a specified QE day; and
-- src:1014 | (b) the superannuation guarantee charge payable on the shortfall.
@ref s 36(1), (2) (src:1012-1014)
-- src:1015 | (2) The Commissioner may make such an assessment:
-- src:1016 | (a) based on information in a voluntary disclosure statement lodged by the employer for the QE day; or
-- src:1017 | (b) on the Commissioner’s own initiative.
-- src:1018 | When a deeming rule applies for working out any individual notional earnings component in an assessment
@ref s 36(1), (2) (src:1015-1018)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner may at any time make an assessment of the shortfall and the charge payable on it` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- 36(4): the charge in relation to an assessment is payable on the day the assessment is made.
-- src:1027 | (4) Superannuation guarantee charge in relation to such an assessment is payable on the day that the assessment is made.
@ref s 36(4) (src:1027-1027)
GIVEN `the day the assessment is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day charge in relation to an assessment is payable` MEANS `the day the assessment is made`

-- src:1029 | (1) The Commissioner may, subject to this section, at any time amend any assessment by making any alterations or additions that the Commissioner thinks necessary, whether or not superannuation guarantee charge has been paid in relation to the assessment.
@ref s 37(1) (src:1029-1029)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner may at any time amend an assessment, whether or not charge has been paid` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- 37(2): where there has been an avoidance of charge: at any time if the Commissioner is of the opinion that it is due to fraud or evasion; otherwise within 4 years from the day the assessment is made.
-- src:1030 | (2) Subject to this section, if there has been an avoidance of superannuation guarantee charge, the Commissioner may:
-- src:1031 | (a) if the Commissioner is of the opinion that the avoidance of the charge is due to fraud or evasion—at any time; or
-- src:1032 | (b) in any other case—within 4 years from the day on which the assessment is made;
-- src:1033 | amend the assessment by making any alterations or additions that the Commissioner thinks necessary to correct the assessment.
@ref s 37(2) (src:1030-1033)
GIVEN `there has been an avoidance of superannuation guarantee charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is of the opinion that the avoidance is due to fraud or evasion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the amendment` IS A DATE
      `the day the assessment is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner may amend the assessment to correct an avoidance` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`there has been an avoidance of superannuation guarantee charge`) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the Commissioner is of the opinion that the avoidance is due to fraud or evasion` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE `an act is within n years from an event` `the day of the amendment` `the day the assessment is made` 4

-- 37(3), (5), (6): a reduction is not effective unless made within 4 years from the day the assessment was made; (5) an application within 4 years of the day charge became payable, with all information lodged within that period, may be given effect even after it; (6) giving effect to a review, appeal or objection.
-- src:1034 | (3) An amendment effecting a reduction in an employer’s liability under an assessment is not effective unless it is made within 4 years from the day on which the assessment was made.
@ref s 37(3), (5), (6) (src:1034-1034)
-- src:1036 | (5) If:
-- src:1037 | (a) an employer applies for an amendment of the employer’s assessment within 4 years from the day that superannuation guarantee charge became payable under the assessment; and
-- src:1038 | (b) within that period, the employer lodges all information the Commissioner needs to decide the application;
-- src:1039 | the Commissioner may amend the assessment when considering the application, even if that period has elapsed.
@ref s 37(3), (5), (6) (src:1036-1039)
-- src:1040 | (6) Nothing in this section prevents the amendment of an assessment to give effect to:
-- src:1041 | (a) the decision on any review or appeal; or
-- src:1042 | (b) its amendment by reduction of any particular following the employer’s objection or pending any review or appeal.
@ref s 37(3), (5), (6) (src:1040-1042)
GIVEN `the day of the amendment` IS A DATE
      `the day the assessment was made` IS A DATE
      `the employer applied within 4 years from the day charge became payable and lodged all the information needed within that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment gives effect to the decision on a review or appeal, or follows the employer's objection or is pending a review or appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an amendment effecting a reduction in the liability is effective` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the employer applied within 4 years from the day charge became payable and lodged all the information needed within that period` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the amendment gives effect to the decision on a review or appeal, or follows the employer's objection or is pending a review or appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE `an act is within n years from an event` `the day of the amendment` `the day the assessment was made` 4

-- src:1035 | (4) If an assessment has, under this section, been amended in any particular, the Commissioner may, within 4 years from the day on which superannuation guarantee charge became payable under the amended assessment, make, in or in relation to the particular, any further amendment in the assessment that, in the Commissioner’s opinion, is necessary to effect such reduction in the employer’s liability under the assessment as is just.
@ref s 37(4) (src:1035-1035)
GIVEN `the day of the further amendment` IS A DATE
      `the day charge became payable under the amended assessment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner may make a further amendment to reduce the liability` MEANS
    `an act is within n years from an event` `the day of the further amendment` `the day charge became payable under the amended assessment` 4

-- src:1043 | (7) Superannuation guarantee charge under an amended assessment is taken to have become payable on the day on which charge under the original assessment became payable.
@ref s 37(7) (src:1043-1043)
GIVEN `the day charge under the original assessment became payable` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day charge under an amended assessment is taken to have become payable` MEANS `the day charge under the original assessment became payable`

-- src:1045 | (1) If, because an assessment is amended, a person’s liability to superannuation guarantee charge is reduced:
-- src:1046 | (a) the amount by which the charge is reduced is taken, for the purposes of section 49, never to have been payable; and
-- src:1047 | (b) the Commissioner must:
-- src:1048 | (i) refund any overpaid amount; or
-- src:1049 | (ii) apply any overpaid amount against the person’s liability (if any) to the Commonwealth and refund any part of the amount that is not so applied.
@ref s 38 (src:1045-1049)
-- src:1050 | (2) In this section:
-- src:1051 | overpaid amount includes each of the following:
-- src:1052 | (a) any overpaid amount of superannuation guarantee charge in the form of general interest charge that became payable under section 49;
-- src:1053 | (b) if the reduction in the liability results in an amended penalty assessment of an administrative penalty—any overpayment of the administrative penalty;
-- src:1054 | (c) any overpayment of administrative penalty under Part 4-25 in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953 relating to the reduction in the liability.
@ref s 38 (src:1050-1054)
GIVEN `the overpaid amount before the listed components` IS A NUMBER
      `overpaid general interest charge that became payable under section 49` IS A NUMBER
      `overpayment of an administrative penalty under an amended penalty assessment` IS A NUMBER
      `overpayment of administrative penalty under Part 4-25 in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the overpaid amount` MEANS
    (`the overpaid amount before the listed components` PLUS `overpaid general interest charge that became payable under section 49`) PLUS (`overpayment of an administrative penalty under an amended penalty assessment` PLUS `overpayment of administrative penalty under Part 4-25 in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953`)

-- 38(1)(b): the Commissioner must (i) refund any overpaid amount, or (ii) apply it against the person's liability to the Commonwealth and refund the rest. The text does not say which limb applies; both give the same refund when there is no such liability.
-- src:1045 | (1) If, because an assessment is amended, a person’s liability to superannuation guarantee charge is reduced:
-- src:1046 | (a) the amount by which the charge is reduced is taken, for the purposes of section 49, never to have been payable; and
-- src:1047 | (b) the Commissioner must:
-- src:1048 | (i) refund any overpaid amount; or
-- src:1049 | (ii) apply any overpaid amount against the person’s liability (if any) to the Commonwealth and refund any part of the amount that is not so applied.
@ref s 38(1)(b) (src:1045-1049)
GIVEN `the overpaid amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the liability of the person to the Commonwealth` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount the Commissioner must refund` MEANS
    IF `the liability of the person to the Commonwealth` AT MOST 0
    THEN JUST `the overpaid amount`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1045 | (1) If, because an assessment is amended, a person’s liability to superannuation guarantee charge is reduced:
-- src:1046 | (a) the amount by which the charge is reduced is taken, for the purposes of section 49, never to have been payable; and
-- src:1047 | (b) the Commissioner must:
-- src:1048 | (i) refund any overpaid amount; or
-- src:1049 | (ii) apply any overpaid amount against the person’s liability (if any) to the Commonwealth and refund any part of the amount that is not so applied.
@ref s 38(1)(b)(ii) (src:1045-1049)
GIVEN `the overpaid amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the liability of the person to the Commonwealth` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount applied against the liability to the Commonwealth under limb (ii)` MEANS
    IF `the liability of the person to the Commonwealth` GREATER THAN `the overpaid amount` THEN `the overpaid amount` ELSE IF `the liability of the person to the Commonwealth` AT MOST 0 THEN 0 ELSE `the liability of the person to the Commonwealth`

-- src:1045 | (1) If, because an assessment is amended, a person’s liability to superannuation guarantee charge is reduced:
-- src:1046 | (a) the amount by which the charge is reduced is taken, for the purposes of section 49, never to have been payable; and
-- src:1047 | (b) the Commissioner must:
-- src:1048 | (i) refund any overpaid amount; or
-- src:1049 | (ii) apply any overpaid amount against the person’s liability (if any) to the Commonwealth and refund any part of the amount that is not so applied.
@ref s 38(1)(a) (src:1045-1049)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the reduction is taken, for section 49, never to have been payable` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- src:1055 | 39 Amended assessment to be an assessment
-- src:1056 | Except as otherwise expressly provided by this Act, an amended assessment is taken to be an assessment for all the purposes of this Act.
@ref s 39 (src:1055-1056)
GIVEN `the Act expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an amended assessment is taken to be an assessment for all the purposes of the Act` MEANS
    IF `the Act expressly provides otherwise` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1057 | 40 Notice of assessment or amendment
-- src:1058 | As soon as practicable after an assessment is made under section 36 or is amended under section 37, the Commissioner must give written notice of the assessment or amendment (as the case may be) to the person liable to pay the superannuation guarantee charge.
@ref s 40 (src:1057-1058)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner must give written notice of the assessment or amendment to the person liable as soon as practicable` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- src:1059 | 41 Validity of assessment
-- src:1060 | The validity of an assessment is not affected because any provision of this Act has not been complied with.
@ref s 41 (src:1059-1060)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`non-compliance with a provision of this Act affects an assessment` MEANS JUST FALSE

-- src:1061 | 42 Objections against assessment
-- src:1062 | An employer who is dissatisfied with an assessment may object in the manner set out in Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953.
@ref s 42 (src:1061-1062)
GIVEN `the employer is dissatisfied with an assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer may object in the manner set out in Part IVC of the Taxation Administration Act 1953` MEANS
    IF `the employer is dissatisfied with an assessment` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Part 5: administration (sections 43 and 44)`

-- src:1064 | 43 General administration of Act
-- src:1065 | The Commissioner has the general administration of this Act.
-- src:1066 | Note: An effect of this provision is that people who acquire information under this Act are subject to the confidentiality obligations and exceptions in Division 355 in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953.
@ref s 43 (src:1064-1066)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner has the general administration of this Act` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- src:1067 | 44 Annual report
-- src:1068 | After the end of each year, the Commissioner must give the Treasurer a report on the working of this Act during the year for presentation to the Parliament.
@ref s 44 (src:1067-1068)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner must give the Treasurer a report on the working of this Act after the end of each year` MEANS JUST TRUE

§ `Part 6: unpaid charge (section 49)`

-- src:1071 | (1) If any of the superannuation guarantee charge which an employer is liable to pay remains unpaid after the time by which it is due to be paid, the employer is liable to pay the general interest charge on the unpaid amount (the original unpaid amount).
-- src:1072 | Note: The general interest charge is worked out under Part IIA of the Taxation Administration Act 1953.
@ref s 49(1) (src:1071-1072)
GIVEN `any of the charge the employer is liable to pay remains unpaid after the time by which it is due to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer is liable to pay general interest charge on the unpaid amount` MEANS
    IF `any of the charge the employer is liable to pay remains unpaid after the time by which it is due to be paid` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1073 | (3) The employer is liable to pay the general interest charge for each day in the period that:
-- src:1074 | (a) started at the beginning of the day by which the superannuation guarantee charge was due to be paid; and
-- src:1075 | (b) finishes at the end of the last day on which, at the end of the day, any of the following remains unpaid:
-- src:1076 | (i) the superannuation guarantee charge;
-- src:1077 | (ii) general interest charge on any of the superannuation guarantee charge.
@ref s 49(3), (4) (src:1073-1077)
-- src:1078 | (4) The amount of the general interest charge is taken to be superannuation guarantee charge payable under this section.
@ref s 49(3), (4) (src:1078-1078)
GIVEN `the day the charge was due to be paid` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which, at the end of the day, any of it remains unpaid` IS A DATE
      `the general interest charge for each day in the period, worked out under Part IIA of the Taxation Administration Act 1953` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the general interest charge payable under section 49` MEANS
    IF count `the general interest charge for each day in the period, worked out under Part IIA of the Taxation Administration Act 1953` EQUALS `the number of days for which general interest charge is payable` `the day the charge was due to be paid` `the last day on which, at the end of the day, any of it remains unpaid`
    THEN JUST (`the sum of a list` `the general interest charge for each day in the period, worked out under Part IIA of the Taxation Administration Act 1953`)
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN amounts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum of a list` MEANS
    CONSIDER amounts
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN a FOLLOWED BY rest THEN a PLUS `the sum of a list` rest

§ `Part 6: public officers and service (sections 57 to 58)`

DECLARE `Where a notice is given or served` IS ONE OF
    `at the address for service of the public officer, or on the public officer`
    `on a person acting or appearing to act in the business, there being no public officer`
    `on a director, the secretary or another officer of the company`
    `on an attorney or agent of the company or trustee`
    `somewhere else`

-- src:1081 | (2) Service of a notice or other document at the public officer’s address for service, or on the public officer, is sufficient service on the company for the purposes of this Act, but, if at any time there is no public officer of the company, service on a person acting or appearing to act in the business of the company is sufficient.
-- src:1082 | Note: See section 57A for alternative ways to give a notice to, or serve another document on, a company (through its officers, attorneys or agents).
@ref s 57(2), 57A, 58(2), (7) (src:1081-1082)
-- src:1087 | 57A Notifying and serving companies
-- src:1088 | For the purposes of this Act, if the Commissioner thinks fit, a notice or process may be given to, or served on, a company by giving the notice to, or serving the process on:
-- src:1089 | (a) a director, the secretary or another officer of the company; or
-- src:1090 | (b) an attorney or agent of the company.
-- src:1091 | Note: See subsection 57(2) for alternative ways to serve a notice or another document on a company (through its public officer or someone else acting or appearing to act for the company).
@ref s 57(2), 57A, 58(2), (7) (src:1087-1091)
-- src:1094 | (2) Service of a notice or other document at the public officer’s address for service, or on the public officer, is sufficient service on the trustee of the trust estate for the purposes of this Act, but, if at any time there is no public officer of the trust estate, service on a person acting or appearing to act in the business of the trust estate is sufficient.
@ref s 57(2), 57A, 58(2), (7) (src:1094-1094)
-- src:1099 | (7) Despite subsections (1) to (6) (inclusive) and without affecting any of the public officer’s obligations and liabilities, a notice, process or proceeding that under this Act may be given to, served on or brought against the trustee or public officer of the trust estate may, if the Commissioner thinks fit, be given to, served on or brought against any agent or attorney of the trustee, and the agent or attorney has the same liability in relation to the notice, process or proceeding as the trustee or public officer would have had if it had been given to, served on or brought against the trustee or public officer.
@ref s 57(2), 57A, 58(2), (7) (src:1099-1099)
GIVEN where IS A `Where a notice is given or served`
      `the Commissioner thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`giving a notice or serving a document is sufficient service` MEANS
    CONSIDER where
    WHEN `at the address for service of the public officer, or on the public officer` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `on a person acting or appearing to act in the business, there being no public officer` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `on a director, the secretary or another officer of the company` THEN IF `the Commissioner thinks fit` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `on an attorney or agent of the company or trustee` THEN IF `the Commissioner thinks fit` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `somewhere else` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1080 | (1) The person who is, from time to time, the public officer of a company for the purposes of section 252 of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1936 is the public officer of the company for the purposes of this Act, and the public officer’s address for service under that Act is the public officer’s address for service under this Act.
@ref s 57(1), 58(1) (src:1080-1080)
-- src:1093 | (1) The person who is, from time to time, the public officer of a trust estate for the purposes of section 252A of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1936 is the public officer of the trust estate for the purposes of this Act, and the public officer’s address for service under that Act is the public officer’s address for service under this Act.
@ref s 57(1), 58(1) (src:1093-1093)
GIVEN `the person is the public officer for the purposes of section 252 or 252A of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1936` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person is the public officer for the purposes of this Act` MEANS
    IF `the person is the public officer for the purposes of section 252 or 252A of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1936` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1083 | (3) The public officer is answerable for doing all acts required to be done by the company under this Act, and in case of default is liable to the same penalties.
@ref s 57(3), (4), 58(3), (4) (src:1083-1083)
-- src:1084 | (4) Everything done by the public officer that the public officer is required to do in that capacity is taken to have been done by the company.
@ref s 57(3), (4), 58(3), (4) (src:1084-1084)
-- src:1095 | (3) The public officer is answerable for doing all acts required to be done by the trustee of the trust estate under this Act, and in case of default is liable to the same penalties.
@ref s 57(3), (4), 58(3), (4) (src:1095-1095)
-- src:1096 | (4) Everything done by the public officer that the public officer is required to do in that capacity is taken to have been done by the trustee of the trust estate.
@ref s 57(3), (4), 58(3), (4) (src:1096-1096)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the public officer is answerable for the acts required of the company or trustee and is liable to the same penalties` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- src:1085 | (5) If, at any time, there is no public officer of the company, this Act applies in relation to the company as if there were no requirement to appoint a public officer of the company.
@ref s 57(5), 58(5) (src:1085-1085)
-- src:1097 | (5) If, at any time, there is no public officer of the trust estate, this Act applies in relation to the trustee of the trust estate as if there were no requirement to appoint a public officer of the trust estate.
@ref s 57(5), 58(5) (src:1097-1097)
GIVEN `there is no public officer at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Act applies as if there were no requirement to appoint a public officer` MEANS
    IF `there is no public officer at the time` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1086 | (6) A proceeding under this Act brought against the public officer is taken to have been brought against the company, and the company is liable jointly with the public officer for any penalty imposed on the public officer.
@ref s 57(6), 58(6) (src:1086-1086)
-- src:1098 | (6) A proceeding under this Act brought against the public officer is taken to have been brought against the trustee of the trust estate, and the trustee is liable jointly with the public officer for any penalty imposed on the public officer.
@ref s 57(6), 58(6) (src:1098-1098)
GIVEN `a proceeding under this Act is brought against the public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the proceeding is taken to have been brought against the company or trustee, who is liable jointly with the public officer for any penalty` MEANS
    IF `a proceeding under this Act is brought against the public officer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
